-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  std_hookio_stream_text_mode.adam - text mode from C on a virtual file
  and on a real file of the same bytes (PaskalCPP's std_hookio
  TestStreamTextMode)

  Windows: ucrt's text mode; Linux has none, every mode reads and writes
  the bytes as they are. Every sample through "rt", "r" and "rb": every
  read slot equals the real file's (an fscanf among them). The write
  forms through "at", "a" and "ab": the same slots, and the IO holds the
  real file's bytes. "r+t" writing at the end of a text that ends in a
  Ctrl-Z: the same.
*******************************************************************************/

